                    "email": "rohitmohanty5.8.2000@gmail.com",
                    "name": "Rohit"
                },
                "message": "Fix dangling __Pyx_FakeReference for numeric literal in conditional expr assigned into C++ container element (GH-7927)\n\nIntNode.coerce_to() / FloatNode.coerce_to() stamped a C++ reference target\ntype (e.g. the 'int&' returned by vector::operator[]) onto the literal\ninstead of stripping it, the way the base ExprNode.coerce_to() does for\nevery other node. So 'container[i] = 1 if cond else 2' gave the ternary\nbranches type 'int&', the spanning type came out as 'int&', and\nanalyse_result_type() turned that into __Pyx_FakeReference<int> -- a temp\nbound to a branch value that dies at the end of the statement, leaving the\nfollowing store to read a dangling pointer.\n\nNon-literal branches were already fine via the base coerce_to().",
